    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who earns our daily top-tier rating of 78.29. His elite sprint speed makes him an essential start, and he benefits from a highly favorable matchup against Bradley, T, where a 14% platoon advantage and the pitcher's slow delivery provide a perfect storm for stolen base production. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a must-start at 72.69; despite a challenging same-handed matchup against Trevor Rogers, his elite .475 xwOBA overrides any platoon concerns, and the favorable SP skill rating suggests he will capitalize on high-leverage opportunities. **Colt Keith** also presents immense value at 69.64, as he exploits a soft matchup against Grayson Rodriguez, gaining a significant boost from a strong batting order placement and favorable park factors.\n\nStrategic lineup construction today heavily weights platoon advantages and situational speed. **Christian Yelich** (62.43) and **Lars Nootbaar** (63.99) are both strong plays, with **Yelich** leveraging a 13% platoon edge despite a tough opponent hold rate, and **Nootbaar** benefiting from an 11% platoon boost against Brandon Pfaadt. We are monitoring the status of **Caleb Durbin** (56.88) and **Junior Caminero** (66.95) closely, as both are currently flagged with a 39% rain risk. While both are productive, the weather volatility adds a layer of caution. **Chase Meidroth** was our most difficult omission, posting a respectable 52.83, but he was ultimately relegated to the bench because his lower lineup projection (assumed #9) capped his run-scoring potential compared to the high-OBP threats currently filling our utility and infield slots. \n\nWe are proceeding with caution regarding our back-end depth, specifically **Dillon Dingler** (51.06) and **Gary Sanchez** (44.31), who are currently sitting in marginal territory. **Nelson Velazquez** (55.30) provides a decent floor, but owners should be ready to pivot if official lineups shift away from our projected spots for **Dillon Dingler** or **Nelson Velazquez**. With the high concentration of speed in **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Trea Turner** (65.78), and **Christian Yelich**, the Zuerich Zebras are well-positioned to dominate the SB category, provided our high-scoring anchors like **Yordan Alvarez** and **Junior Caminero** avoid the rainouts in their respective matchups.",
